[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Ruy Lopez"]
[Variation "Berlin Defence, Endgame"]
[ECO "C67"]
[Character "positional,solid"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "healthy-pawns,bishop-pair"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Nf6 { The Berlin: Black attacks e4 instead of defending e5. }
4. O-O { Castles and lets Black take e4, because White wins the pawn back with d4. } 4... Nxe4 ( 4... d6 5. d4 Bd7 6. Nc3 Be7 7. Bxc6 Bxc6 8. dxe5 dxe5 9. Qxd8+ Bxd8 10. Nxe5 )
5. d4 { Hits the knight on e4 and prepares to open the centre. } 5... Nd6 ( 5... Be7 6. Qe2 Nd6 7. Bxc6 bxc6 8. dxe5 Nb7 9. Nc3 O-O 10. Rd1 )
6. Bxc6 { Trades before the knight on d6 can be supported, and wrecks Black's pawns on the queenside. } 6... dxc6
7. dxe5 { Wins back the pawn and attacks the knight on d6. } 7... Nf5
8. Qxd8+ { Trades queens. Black must recapture with the king and loses the right to castle. } 8... Kxd8
9. Nc3 { Develops with the plan of using White's healthier pawn majority on the kingside. } 9... Ke8
10. h3 { Stops ...Bg4, which would let Black trade a bishop for the knight on f3. } 10... Bd7
11. b3 { Prepares Bb2: the bishop will defend e5 and aim along the long diagonal. } 11... h5
12. Bb2 *
